      "dom_id": "step-q42458",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix given above. Identify **all** of the reasons why one can conclude that $|A|=0?$\n\nI. $A$ has a zero column\n\nII. $A$ has identical columns\n\nIII. $A$ has identical rows",
      "worked_solution": "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- $A$ has a zero column: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\,✓\n$$\n\n- $A$ does *not* have identical columns.\n\n- $A$ has identical rows: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"",
